    "problem_statement": "The network checksum helpers (the IPv4/IPv6 checksum functions and the UDP/ICMP/TCP wrappers built on them) must report a calculation failure as a negative return code while delivering the computed checksum through an output argument, instead of returning 0 (which is itself a valid checksum, e.g. for an empty payload) on error. In addition, the places in the networking stack that move the packet cursor with net_pkt_skip() must handle the error case when the skip fails, rather than silently proceeding with an unpositioned cursor. Callers that previously treated a 0 return as a valid checksum must now check the return code and use the separate checksum output value.",
